Z||000010||Elenor84||03-12-2001||02:07 AM||||I don't think u guys read the post...he didn't say he was racing...he said u wanted to spin his damn tires...now I don't think he's stupid...we all know that spinning tires in a race will slow u down.  But u guys can't tell me that u don't lose it wen u see a car just spinnin the tires with a big clowd of smoke all around his car and hearing that beutiful sound of squeeeeel.  Most of us are probably guys here and we like that...well we should...if not somethings wrong.  I drive a 2.5 and at best I can squak um...but I have sweet new tires but thats not the point...my engine is badly tuned.  For my instence would u guys say just put some bald bald tires on?  Just for fun...I'm not racing or anything...I just want to have that beutiful smoke and squeel...?  Thx!<P>Sorry to go all hard core on u guys but comon...burnin rubber is the best!  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||6
Z||000011||Conrad Sanville||03-12-2001||06:27 AM||||<BR>If one wants to burn rubber and do smoke shows get a front-wheel-drive and set the parking brake.  Mid-engined cars have a lot more traction on take off due to the rear weight bias. Any of the engines that GM used in the Fiero will smoke the wheels on its FWD cousins.                                                         I think the front-end lift that the Fiero has on take off is much more impressive. Only problem with dogging the cars is that it raises hell with the toe-link rods and engine mounts.<P>My neighbors are much more impressed when they see one of my Fieros headed up a steep snowy grade in the winter.  Amazing traction going up hills with some good snow tires all way-round.||||reg||1
Z||000012||GT Bastard||03-12-2001||07:30 AM||||Finally someone mentions the factor of the weight resting on the rear end.  That's the whole key.  My old 2.8 Camaro with an auto would burn off the tires.  Not because it had power, but because the rear end was light.||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||03-12-2001||08:33 AM||||If your just looking to do a burn out to heat up tires.. or just to kill mosquitos  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> yeah.. Mine will. Drop it down into 1st STAND on the brake and PUNCH the gas... DON'T roll in the gas slowly, slam it to the floor. then try to keep it straight... with the new exhaust and the shift kit it'll chirp 2nd @ the shift.||||reg||1
Z||000014||stsmithgt||03-12-2001||11:59 AM||||Wait for a rainy day if you want to play....Or! use a little additive(of your choice) on those tires if you want to spin tires and see smoke. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Hey hey! #500 post!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Matt Hawkins||03-12-2001||01:31 PM||||One thing to remember is tire quality.  I had some cheap Cooper Cobras and I could spin those all day long.  I got a good set of summer only Sumitomos and can just barely turn them over unless I am seriously abusing the car.  This is with a V-6 5-speed.  The difference in traction with good tires is tremendous.||||reg||1
